/* LISTENING (supplément 1) — Listen and Choose a Response + annonces. Ajout via push. */
CONTENT.lcr.push(
  { id: "lx001", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "I'm heading down to the café to grab a sandwich. Can I get you anything?", o: ["The café closes at three on Fridays.", "I grabbed one there earlier, and it was good.", "A coffee would be great, if it's no trouble.", "Yes, they're making fresh sandwiches downstairs."], a: 2, x: "Offre → on accepte et on précise ce que l'on veut. Les autres réponses ignorent la proposition." },
  { id: "lx002", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Has Professor Lang posted the midterm grades yet?", o: ["Yes, I posted a comment on the forum last night.", "The midterm covers the first six chapters.", "I checked the portal an hour ago, and nothing yet.", "I'm hoping for a decent grade, to be honest."], a: 2, x: "Question sur un fait récent → vérification récente et « nothing yet »." },
  { id: "lx003", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "They're saying the strike could drag on for weeks.", o: ["The strike notice went out last Tuesday.", "That would throw the whole semester off track.", "I walked past the picket line this morning.", "Most unions are in favor of that."], a: 1, x: "Information alarmante → commentaire sur les conséquences. Les autres réponses sont hors sujet ou contredisent le sens." },
  { id: "lx004", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "I wish you'd told me you were stopping by.", o: ["Please do stop by whenever you like.", "I wish the weather had been nicer, too.", "Sorry, it was a last-minute decision, and I didn't want to bother you.", "I think the bakery on Elm Street is better."], a: 2, x: "Reproche (« I wish you'd… ») → excuse et justification." },
  { id: "lx005", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "I overslept and missed the whole first lecture, and now I'm hopelessly behind.", o: ["Don't worry, I can lend you my notes.", "I've always been an early riser myself.", "The lecture hall is on the second floor.", "Yes, the professor is behind schedule too."], a: 0, x: "Problème → offre d'aide concrète." },
  { id: "lx006", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "We were hoping you could shed some light on the situation.", o: ["Sure, let me walk you through what happened.", "We'd been hoping for a better outcome as well.", "It's too dark in here to see anything, isn't it?", "I'm afraid the lamp isn't working."], a: 0, x: "« shed light on » = éclaircir → on propose d'expliquer. Les autres lisent l'expression au sens propre." },
  { id: "lx007", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "Do you think we should call the landlord about the heating?", o: ["The landlord lives in the building next door.", "Yes, it's been broken for three days now.", "I'd rather not rent in that neighborhood.", "It was hot enough in here yesterday."], a: 1, x: "Question d'avis → réponse positive justifiée par un fait." },
  { id: "lx008", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "If you're not busy, could you give me a hand moving this desk?", o: ["The desk is much too heavy for me.", "I'd like to move the desk by the window.", "I broke my hand last year.", "Sure, just let me put my bag down."], a: 3, x: "Demande polie → accord. Les autres réponses ne répondent pas à la demande." },
  { id: "lx009", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "Don't get me wrong, I like Mark, but he's not right for this role.", o: ["I see your point. What kind of person do you have in mind?", "I like the role, too, but it pays badly.", "Mark has been working here for three years.", "I didn't get the wrong change, though."], a: 0, x: "« Don't get me wrong » introduit une critique nuancée → on demande de préciser." },
  { id: "lx010", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "I'm trying to get a refund for this printer. It stopped working after two days.", o: ["Yes, it prints very well for its price.", "I tried to print the document twice.", "Do you have the receipt with you?", "A good printer is a smart investment."], a: 2, x: "Contexte service client → question de vérification (preuve d'achat)." },
  { id: "lx011", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "Do you happen to know where I'm supposed to turn in my scholarship application?", o: ["It's due at the end of October.", "I turned left at the corner.", "The application was longer than I expected.", "At the admissions office, window three, I believe."], a: 3, x: "« Where » → un lieu. « It's due… » répond à « when »." },
  { id: "lx012", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "Sorry I'm late, the bus broke down halfway here.", o: ["Yes, it was a very old bus.", "No problem, we've only just started.", "The class is down the hall.", "You should have taken a taxi."], a: 1, x: "Excuse → réaction rassurante. Le reproche final ne convient pas au registre." },
  { id: "lx013", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "Who's giving the keynote talk this afternoon?", o: ["At three o'clock in the main auditorium.", "Some professor from Oxford, I think.", "It's supposed to be a very long talk.", "I'll be talking to my roommate then."], a: 1, x: "« Who » → une personne. La première réponse correspond à « when / where »." },
  { id: "lx014", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "She's been under the weather all week.", o: ["It's been unusually rainy lately.", "I hope she's feeling better soon.", "She was caught in the rain on Monday.", "It's the weather forecast that worries me."], a: 1, x: "« under the weather » = patraque → réaction empathique. Les autres lisent l'idiome littéralement." },
  { id: "lx015", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "Could I get an itemized receipt, please?", o: ["I received the package last week.", "The recipe is on the back of the box.", "It was a great deal for the price.", "Of course, give me a second to print it."], a: 3, x: "Demande de service → accord. Piège sonore : « receipt / recipe »." },
  { id: "lx016", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Do you know if the pharmacy on Main Street delivers?", o: ["They do, but only within two miles.", "No, I'm not a delivery driver.", "It was founded in nineteen ninety.", "I got my prescription yesterday."], a: 0, x: "« Do you know if » → information factuelle avec une nuance." },
  { id: "lx017", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "We'd better get going if we don't want to miss the opening remarks.", o: ["I wrote my remarks down last night.", "I'd rather stay for the closing ceremony.", "Right, I'll text Tom and tell him to meet us there.", "We didn't miss anything, thankfully."], a: 2, x: "« We'd better » = urgence → on agit." },
  { id: "lx018", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Have you been to the new sports center yet?", o: ["Not yet, but I'm planning to go on Saturday.", "Sports are very popular in my country.", "The membership costs thirty dollars a month.", "I went there for the first time last year."], a: 0, x: "Question au present perfect → « Not yet » + projet. La dernière réponse est incohérente : le centre est neuf." },
  { id: "lx019", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "How long have you been living in this neighborhood?", o: ["I live in a shared apartment.", "Since I started college, so almost three years.", "For about ten dollars a week.", "It's a long street, isn't it?"], a: 1, x: "« How long have you… » → durée avec « since / for »." },
  { id: "lx020", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "Do you have a minute to talk about my paper?", o: ["It's one minute past three.", "Sure, come by my office after lunch.", "I talked about it with my advisor already.", "The paper is due on Friday."], a: 1, x: "Demande d'entretien → accord + moment." },
  { id: "lx021", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Would it be possible to reschedule my appointment for next week?", o: ["How about Wednesday at two instead?", "It's impossible to schedule anything now.", "I'm afraid I was late for it.", "Yes, the appointment was yesterday."], a: 0, x: "Demande polie → contre-proposition d'horaire." },
  { id: "lx022", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "I'd hate to think what would've happened if we'd missed the flight.", o: ["I hate flying as much as you do.", "Don't even go there. Let's just be glad we made it.", "We had already missed lunch anyway.", "The flight left on time, as always."], a: 1, x: "Hypothèse sur le passé (3e conditionnel) → apaisement." },
  { id: "lx023", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "Not to be rude, but I think you've got the wrong room.", o: ["I'm not being rude at all.", "I shared a room with her last year.", "Thanks, I will be on time next week.", "Oh no, you're right. I'm so embarrassed."], a: 3, x: "Remarque polie → gêne et correction. Les autres réponses ignorent la remarque." },
  { id: "lx024", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "Would you say the proposal is more or less ready to submit?", o: ["More or less, though the budget section still needs a final pass.", "I'd say we should celebrate.", "It runs to ten pages, including the appendix.", "The proposal was rejected last time."], a: 0, x: "Réponse nuancée (« more or less, though… »)." },
  { id: "lx025", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "How come the cafeteria is closed so early today?", o: ["I got there in time for lunch.", "It was a close call between the two.", "There's a staff meeting this afternoon.", "The cafeteria was cleaned last week."], a: 2, x: "« How come » = pourquoi → raison." },
  { id: "lx026", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Excuse me, is this café self-service, or will someone come to take our order?", o: ["Yes, I serve myself dinner at home.", "The coffee is excellent here.", "A waiter will be with you in a minute.", "There's a service charge on the bill."], a: 2, x: "Question à deux options → on choisit : serveur." },
  { id: "lx027", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "If it were up to me, I'd move the deadline to next month.", o: ["Unfortunately, it's not up to either of us.", "I'm up to my neck in work as well.", "Next month is already October.", "The movers are arriving at noon."], a: 0, x: "Hypothèse irréelle → rappel de la réalité." },
  { id: "lx028", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Excuse me, can I pay by check?", o: ["I'm sorry, we only accept cash or card.", "Yes, I checked the price twice.", "The payment was late again.", "A check mark is fine."], a: 0, x: "Question de possibilité → refus poli. Piège : « check » répété." },
  { id: "lx029", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "The cafeteria ran out of vegetarian options by noon.", o: ["They should order more, then.", "Noon is when most people eat.", "I'm running out of time too.", "The vegetables looked fresh."], a: 0, x: "Constat → commentaire logique." },
  { id: "lx030", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "Is the museum free on Sundays?", o: ["The museum has a new exhibit.", "Only after two in the afternoon.", "Sundays are my days off.", "It's closed on Mondays."], a: 1, x: "Question oui/non → réponse partielle précise." },
  { id: "lx031", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "I'd love to help, but my hands are tied.", o: ["I understand. I'll ask someone else.", "Then wash your hands first.", "Yes, help is badly needed.", "I tied the boxes up this morning."], a: 0, x: "« my hands are tied » = je n'y peux rien → on comprend et on cherche ailleurs." },
  { id: "lx032", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "I took the liberty of booking us a table for eight.", o: ["Liberty is a famous statue.", "I tabled the discussion until later.", "I enjoyed the book very much.", "That's very thoughtful of you, thank you."], a: 3, x: "« take the liberty of » = prendre l'initiative → remerciement." },
  { id: "lx033", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "The projector in room two isn't working again.", o: ["I projected the film last night.", "Room two is bigger than room three.", "I'll ask the technician to take a look.", "It works fine for me."], a: 2, x: "Signalement de problème → action." },
  { id: "lx034", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "You should really get that cough checked out.", o: ["I checked out two library books.", "I know. I keep putting it off.", "I picked it up at the pharmacy.", "I coughed all night, too."], a: 1, x: "Conseil → aveu de procrastination (« put off »)." },
  { id: "lx035", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "I'm inclined to go with the cheaper option.", o: ["Even if it means a longer delivery time?", "Then we'll have to pay for the premium plan.", "Good idea. Let's pick the pricier one, then.", "I declined that option last week."], a: 0, x: "« I'm inclined to » = je penche pour → question pertinente sur le compromis." },
  { id: "lx036", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "I'll start with the soup, and my friend will have the Caesar salad.", o: ["I'll bring you the check in a few minutes.", "Our soup of the day is tomato.", "Yes, my friend loves salad, too.", "Would you like anything to drink with that?"], a: 3, x: "Contexte restaurant → suite logique du serveur." },
  { id: "lx037", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "I wonder if I should have double-checked the address before sending the package.", o: ["You should have sent it by express mail.", "The package weighed about two kilos.", "I wonder where the nearest post office is.", "It's not too late. You can call the courier now."], a: 3, x: "Doute → solution pratique." },
  { id: "lx038", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "I can never remember which floor the computer lab is on.", o: ["The lab report is due on Friday.", "The lab fee is thirty dollars.", "I think it closes at nine tonight.", "It's in the basement, next to the print shop."], a: 3, x: "Réponse directe donnant l'étage. Les autres reprennent « lab » ou répondent à une autre question." },
  { id: "lx039", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "I haven't the faintest idea where I put the receipt.", o: ["I'll have the receipt ready by tomorrow.", "I put mine in the drawer, too.", "Try retracing your steps from this morning.", "I have no idea what the receipt was for."], a: 2, x: "« haven't the faintest idea » = aucune idée → conseil pratique." },
  { id: "lx040", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Do you know whether the shuttle runs on holidays?", o: ["It runs every twenty minutes during the day.", "I believe it's on a reduced schedule. Check the website.", "Yes, the holidays are mostly in December.", "I'm not sure where the shuttle stops."], a: 1, x: "Question indirecte (« whether ») → information nuancée." },
  { id: "lx041", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "I'm wondering whether it'd be worth buying the textbook new.", o: ["It cost me about eighty dollars last year.", "I wonder whether the bookstore delivers.", "The new edition comes out in January.", "If I were you, I'd look for a used copy first."], a: 3, x: "Question hésitante → conseil (« If I were you »)." },
  { id: "lx042", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "This coffee tastes awful, and it's barely warm.", o: ["I'd love some sugar with that.", "Yes, I'll have the same, please.", "The coffee shop closes at six.", "I'm so sorry. Let me get you a fresh cup."], a: 3, x: "Plainte → excuse et solution du serveur." },
  { id: "lx043", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "I'm up to my ears in paperwork this week.", o: ["Want me to take some of it off your hands?", "I'm up to date with everything.", "I'm up to chapter five.", "The paperwork is due on Friday."], a: 0, x: "Idiome (« up to my ears ») → offre d'aide." },
  { id: "lx044", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "Do you know when the bank opens on Saturdays?", o: ["Banks usually open accounts for students.", "It was open until six yesterday.", "I know the manager personally.", "I think at nine, but let me check."], a: 3, x: "« When » → une heure. « Do you know » appelle une information, pas un simple « oui »." },
  { id: "lx045", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "The bus was packed again this morning.", o: ["Maybe we should leave a little earlier tomorrow.", "I packed a lunch for the trip.", "It was snowing in the morning.", "The bus is always on time, though."], a: 0, x: "Constat → suggestion pratique." },
  { id: "lx046", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "Is it okay if I submit the form tomorrow?", o: ["I submitted it twice already.", "The form is available at the front desk.", "I'll fill it out when I get home.", "The deadline is today, I'm afraid."], a: 3, x: "Demande de report → refus poli." },
  { id: "lx047", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Why don't you try the tutoring center?", o: ["The center opened in 2019, I think.", "Yes, I'm trying to finish it by Friday.", "That's a good idea. Do I need an appointment?", "It's not the reason I came today."], a: 2, x: "« Why don't you… » = suggestion → réaction + question pratique." },
  { id: "lx048", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "I'm new in town. How far is the nearest subway station from here?", o: ["Just a five-minute walk.", "Yes, the subway is faster.", "It was far too crowded.", "The station opened last year."], a: 0, x: "« How far » → une distance." },
  { id: "lx049", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "You're going to love this restaurant.", o: ["It's on Elm Street, near the bank.", "I've heard great things about it.", "I'll be late if we don't hurry.", "I loved it last time."], a: 1, x: "Promesse → réaction enthousiaste. « last time » contredit le fait que ce soit une première visite." },
  { id: "lx050", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Do you need a ride to the airport on Friday?", o: ["That would be great. My flight is at seven.", "The airport is about forty minutes away.", "I took a taxi there last week.", "I rode with Tom to the airport last time."], a: 0, x: "Offre → acceptation + raison." },
  { id: "lx051", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "Would you rather work in a group or on your own?", o: ["Yes, I'd rather work on Fridays.", "My group is meeting at four.", "I work at the bank part-time.", "Honestly, I get more done on my own."], a: 3, x: "« Would you rather » → une préférence." },
  { id: "lx052", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "I take issue with the way the survey was conducted.", o: ["The survey is available in several languages.", "The results are due on Friday.", "I conducted it myself last year.", "What exactly bothers you about it?"], a: 3, x: "« take issue with » = contester → question de précision." },
  { id: "lx053", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Are you using this chair, or can I borrow it for a minute?", o: ["It's the only chair that doesn't wobble.", "I used it earlier, but it's uncomfortable.", "No, go ahead and take it.", "Yes, a chair is very useful."], a: 2, x: "Question à deux options → réponse brève et directe." },
  { id: "lx054", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Did you finish the reading for tomorrow's seminar?", o: ["Yes, it was due this morning.", "The reading list is online.", "Not yet. I'm about halfway through.", "The seminar starts at ten."], a: 2, x: "Question sur l'avancement → réponse partielle naturelle." },
  { id: "lx055", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "Rumor has it the cafeteria is switching vendors next term.", o: ["The vendors set up outside on Fridays.", "I hope the new ones have better vegetarian options.", "The cafeteria is on the first floor.", "The term starts in September."], a: 1, x: "« Rumor has it » = on dit que → réaction de souhait." },
  { id: "lx056", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "Could you give me a lift to the station?", o: ["The station closes at midnight.", "I'm afraid I don't own a bike.", "The station is very old.", "Sure, I'm heading that way anyway."], a: 3, x: "« give a lift » = conduire quelqu'un en voiture." },
  { id: "lx057", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "I think there's been a mistake on my bill.", o: ["Let me pull up your account and take a look.", "Our offices are open until five.", "I paid the bill in cash.", "Bills are due on the fifteenth."], a: 0, x: "Réclamation → prise en charge." },
  { id: "lx058", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Would you like some help with those bags? They look heavy.", o: ["That would be great, thanks.", "The help desk is on the second floor.", "They're made of genuine leather.", "No, I really don't like those bags."], a: 0, x: "Offre d'aide → acceptation polie." },
  { id: "lx059", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "I'd like to cancel my gym membership, effective immediately.", o: ["The gym closes at ten on weekdays.", "Certainly. May I have your member number?", "Yes, the membership includes the pool.", "I'll cancel the trip, too."], a: 1, x: "Contexte service client → demande d'identification." },
  { id: "lx060", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "I can't seem to open this file.", o: ["Maybe it's saved in a different format.", "The file cabinet is in the office.", "I seem to have the same file.", "I opened it yesterday, I'm afraid."], a: 0, x: "Problème → hypothèse utile." },
  { id: "lx061", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "I'd appreciate it if you could keep this between us.", o: ["I'll tell everyone as soon as I can.", "Of course. My lips are sealed.", "I appreciate your honesty.", "It's between the library and the gym."], a: 1, x: "Demande de discrétion → promesse (« my lips are sealed »)." },
  { id: "lx062", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Are you going to the review session or studying on your own?", o: ["I reviewed it on my own time.", "The session lasted an hour last time.", "I'll go. The professor said she'd cover the hard topics.", "Studying is hard for everyone."], a: 2, x: "Question à choix → un choix + justification." },
  { id: "lx063", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Can I try this jacket on in a different size?", o: ["Of course. Let me see if we have a medium in stock.", "Yes, it's made of wool.", "The fitting rooms close at nine.", "I tried my best to find one."], a: 0, x: "Contexte magasin : le vendeur vérifie le stock." },
  { id: "lx064", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "It's not that I don't like the idea; it's just that the timing is off.", o: ["So you don't like it at all, then?", "The timing was perfect for me.", "Fair enough. We could revisit it next semester.", "It's not that cold outside, really."], a: 2, x: "Réserve polie → compromis." },
  { id: "lx065", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "I'm pretty sure I aced the interview.", o: ["The interview is next Wednesday.", "I ate chicken for lunch.", "Pretty good, thanks.", "Don't count your chickens before they hatch."], a: 3, x: "Idiome : ne pas vendre la peau de l'ours avant de l'avoir tué." },
  { id: "lx066", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "How soon can you have this ready?", o: ["About fifteen dollars, plus tax.", "I'm already ready, thanks.", "It was ready last week.", "By tomorrow afternoon at the latest."], a: 3, x: "« How soon » → délai." },
  { id: "lx067", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Is there any way I could get an extension on the paper?", o: ["I extended my stay in Boston.", "You'd have to ask the professor, but she's usually flexible.", "Yes, I've got a paper to write.", "The paper is due at noon."], a: 1, x: "Demande indirecte → orientation vers la bonne personne." },
  { id: "lx068", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "May I see your student ID before you go in?", o: ["I saw it on the website.", "Sure, it's in my bag. One second.", "Yes, you may see the doctor.", "I see it clearly, thanks."], a: 1, x: "Demande formelle → accord et petite précision." },
  { id: "lx069", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "Does this bus go downtown?", o: ["It's a new bus line, I think.", "It does, but you'll need to transfer at Elm Street.", "The bus stop is down the street, to the right.", "Yes, but the bus is slow on Fridays."], a: 1, x: "Question oui/non → oui + condition. La dernière option répond « yes » mais décale le sujet sur la vitesse, sans répondre sur le trajet." },
  { id: "lx070", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "How late is the library open tonight?", o: ["It's open to all students.", "It opens at eight on weekdays.", "Until midnight during finals week.", "It has about a million books."], a: 2, x: "« How late » → une heure limite." },
  { id: "lx071", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "The thing is, I've already committed to another project.", o: ["I committed to the project last year, too.", "Projects like this are always boring.", "Then we'd better find someone else for this one.", "The project deadline is on Friday."], a: 2, x: "« The thing is » introduit une objection → adaptation." },
  { id: "lx072", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "I've got two tickets to the game tonight, if you're interested.", o: ["The game starts at seven.", "Really? I'd love to, thanks.", "I'm interested in history, actually.", "Where did you find the time?"], a: 1, x: "Invitation → acceptation enthousiaste." },
  { id: "lx073", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "They've been going back and forth on that decision for weeks.", o: ["Typical. Nobody wants to take responsibility.", "I'm going back and forth between the library and the gym.", "Maybe they went back to the office.", "They should have decided on Monday."], a: 0, x: "« back and forth » = tergiverser → commentaire critique." },
  { id: "lx074", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "Is anyone sitting here, or is this seat free?", o: ["I was sitting here earlier, actually.", "No, it's free. Go ahead.", "Yes, I'm sitting comfortably, thanks.", "It's the best seat in the room."], a: 1, x: "Variante de « Is this seat taken? »" },
  { id: "lx075", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "Do you know the Wi-Fi password for this building?", o: ["I forgot my phone.", "It's on the poster next to the door.", "Yes, the signal is strong.", "The password is very long."], a: 1, x: "Réponse qui oriente vers l'information." },
  { id: "lx076", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "Do you know what time the next train to Chicago leaves?", o: ["It's supposed to be a very fast train.", "At ten fifteen, from platform two.", "I've been to Chicago twice.", "The station is next to the park."], a: 1, x: "« What time » → une heure." },
  { id: "lx077", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "I've been trying to reach you all morning.", o: ["Good morning to you too.", "Sorry, my phone died and I couldn't charge it.", "I reached the office around ten.", "Morning is the best time to call me."], a: 1, x: "Reproche indirect → excuse + explication." },
  { id: "lx078", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "It's a long shot, but it might be worth asking the dean.", o: ["A shot of espresso would do me good.", "You're right. What's the worst that could happen?", "That's a safe bet, then.", "The dean's office is on the second floor."], a: 1, x: "« a long shot » = pari risqué → on encourage à tenter quand même." },
  { id: "lx079", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Let's meet at the cafeteria around one.", o: ["I met her around one yesterday.", "The cafeteria is on the left of the entrance.", "Sounds good. I'll grab us a table by the window.", "It's around the corner from the library."], a: 2, x: "Proposition d'horaire → accord + petite initiative." },
  { id: "lx080", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "Do you have any idea how much it costs to get the transcripts sent overseas?", o: ["The registrar's office is closed on Mondays.", "It usually takes about two weeks to arrive.", "I've been overseas twice for work.", "Last time I paid about thirty dollars, plus shipping."], a: 3, x: "« how much » → un montant. L'autre réponse sur le délai répond à « how long »." },
  { id: "lx081", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "I had no idea the application process would be so involved.", o: ["The process is quite fast, though.", "I applied to three schools last year.", "Yeah, and the essays are the hardest part.", "I had the same idea, actually."], a: 2, x: "Constat → accord et précision. « involved » = long et compliqué." },
  { id: "lx082", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "I thought you were going to join us for dinner.", o: ["I'm glad you enjoyed the dinner.", "I was, but something came up at work.", "I thought it was a great idea, too.", "Please join us next time."], a: 1, x: "Reproche léger → explication (« something came up »)." },
  { id: "lx083", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "I can't tell whether she's joking or not.", o: ["She has a deadline on Friday, so I doubt it.", "With her sense of humor, it's hard to say.", "I didn't hear a word of what she said.", "I told her to stop joking around."], a: 1, x: "Incertitude partagée → écho nuancé." },
  { id: "lx084", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "It goes without saying that the results are preliminary.", o: ["Then they must be final.", "Right, so we shouldn't publish them yet.", "Yes, it was announced yesterday.", "The results were very clear."], a: 1, x: "Rappel prudent (« preliminary » = provisoire) → conclusion logique." },
  { id: "lx085", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "How much do I owe you for my share of the pizza?", o: ["The pizza arrived within half an hour.", "It's about six miles.", "It was delicious, thanks.", "Just ten dollars. I'll cover the rest."], a: 3, x: "« How much » → un montant." },
  { id: "lx086", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "I don't mean to nag, but did you ever send the invoice?", o: ["It's on my to-do list for this afternoon, I promise.", "I'm sure the invoice is correct, as always.", "I never nag anyone, don't worry.", "The invoice was for two hundred dollars."], a: 0, x: "Rappel poli → promesse." },
  { id: "lx087", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Excuse me, is this the line for the ticket office?", o: ["Yes, it starts just behind that sign.", "The tickets were very expensive.", "The ticket office opens at nine.", "I stood in line for an hour yesterday."], a: 0, x: "Question oui/non sur un lieu : confirmation + précision." },
  { id: "lx088", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "I was this close to quitting the team.", o: ["I'm sorry you've left the team.", "The team is close to the finals.", "What changed your mind?", "Then I hope you quit soon."], a: 2, x: "« this close to » = à deux doigts de → question de suivi." },
  { id: "lx089", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "I'm going to have to take a rain check on dinner.", o: ["Sure, let's check the weather first.", "Dinner is at eight at the new place.", "No problem. We'll do it another time.", "I checked out of the hotel this morning."], a: 2, x: "« take a rain check » = reporter l'invitation." },
  { id: "lx090", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Are you free for coffee on Thursday?", o: ["I had coffee with her last Thursday.", "Yes, the café is free on Thursdays.", "Thursday works. How about three o'clock?", "I drink my coffee black."], a: 2, x: "Invitation → acceptation + proposition d'horaire." },
  { id: "lx091", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Do you accept credit cards, or is it cash only?", o: ["The cards are in the display case by the window.", "I took the card back to the bank.", "Yes, but only for amounts over ten dollars.", "I left my wallet in the car."], a: 2, x: "Question à deux options → réponse précise avec condition." },
  { id: "lx092", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "The deadline's coming up fast, and we're nowhere near finished.", o: ["Don't worry, the deadline is next month.", "Coming up with ideas is hard.", "I'm near the building.", "Then let's divide what's left and push through tonight."], a: 3, x: "Constat de retard → plan d'action." },
  { id: "lx093", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "Would you happen to know whether the department offers any funding for conferences?", o: ["Our department head approved the budget last year.", "The conference was in June.", "Yes, I happen to be here.", "Not off the top of my head, but the secretary should know."], a: 3, x: "« off the top of my head » = de mémoire, sans vérifier." },
  { id: "lx094", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "It never occurred to me that the data might be flawed.", o: ["The data were collected last May, as I recall.", "Then there's no point in checking it again.", "It never occurred to me, either.", "We should rerun the analysis to be on the safe side."], a: 3, x: "Réaction scientifique → vérification." },
  { id: "lx095", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "I'm not sure where I should leave my coat.", o: ["I left it in the car, actually.", "It's a wool coat, so it's very warm.", "There's a coat rack by the entrance.", "The cloakroom closes at eight."], a: 2, x: "Demande d'indication → un lieu." },
  { id: "lx096", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "So, what are you majoring in?", o: ["Environmental science, with a minor in economics.", "I'm in my second year.", "It's a major problem, I'm afraid.", "Yes, I've been majoring for two years."], a: 0, x: "« major » = matière principale. Piège : réponse sur l'année d'études." },
  { id: "lx097", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Would you mind taking a quick look at my schedule?", o: ["The schedule is posted on the door.", "I looked at the clock when I arrived.", "I've already looked at mine, thanks.", "Not at all. Let me see what you've got."], a: 3, x: "« Would you mind » → « Not at all » = d'accord." },
  { id: "lx098", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "I just got my midterm back.", o: ["How did you do?", "I got mine back last week.", "The midterm is in March.", "Congratulations on the new job."], a: 0, x: "Annonce → question de suivi naturelle." },
  { id: "lx099", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "How was the exam?", o: ["The exam is on Friday.", "It lasted two hours.", "I'll take it tomorrow.", "Tougher than I expected, but I think I did okay."], a: 3, x: "« How was… » → une impression sur le passé." },
  { id: "lx100", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "I'm sorry to bother you, but you're parked in my spot.", o: ["No bother at all. I'm glad you stopped by.", "Oh, I'm so sorry. I'll move my car right now.", "I didn't bother with the ticket.", "Yes, it's a nice spot, isn't it?"], a: 1, x: "Plainte polie → excuse + action." },
  { id: "lx101", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "How do you like your new apartment?", o: ["I moved there in June.", "It's small, but the location is perfect.", "Yes, apartments are expensive.", "The rent is due on the first."], a: 1, x: "« How do you like… » = qu'en penses-tu ? → une opinion." },
  { id: "lx102", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "He was let off with a warning.", o: ["Lucky him. I would've expected a fine.", "I hope he didn't get fined too much.", "He left a warning on the door.", "Warnings are sent by email these days."], a: 0, x: "« let off with a warning » = s'en tirer avec un avertissement." },
  { id: "lx103", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "Do you have any rooms available this weekend?", o: ["I'm available on Sunday.", "The hotel is near the airport.", "The weekend was relaxing.", "We have one double left, at ninety dollars a night."], a: 3, x: "Contexte hôtel. Piège : « available » répété dans un autre contexte." },
  { id: "lx104", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "I'm so nervous about the presentation.", o: ["You'll be fine. You know the material well.", "I presented it yesterday.", "I'm not nervous at all, to be honest.", "It's very long, isn't it?"], a: 0, x: "Réconfort approprié." },
  { id: "lx105", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "We haven't heard the last of this issue.", o: ["I haven't heard any news about it.", "It's the latest issue of the magazine.", "I wouldn't be surprised if it comes up at the next meeting.", "I heard it on the radio last night."], a: 2, x: "« haven't heard the last of » = ce n'est pas fini." },
  { id: "lx106", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "I'm thinking about taking a gap year.", o: ["Have you talked to your advisor about it yet?", "Gap years are very expensive these days.", "The year is almost over.", "I took the year off last time."], a: 0, x: "Projet annoncé → question de suivi appropriée." },
  { id: "lx107", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Can you recommend a good restaurant around here?", o: ["There's a nice Italian place two blocks down.", "I ate at the new Thai place yesterday.", "The recommendation letter is ready.", "I can't eat out around noon."], a: 0, x: "Demande de recommandation → suggestion concrète." },
  { id: "lx108", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "I wasn't aware that the policy had changed.", o: ["It was announced in an email last week.", "I'm aware of the deadline.", "The policy is fair, in my opinion.", "I changed my mind about it."], a: 0, x: "Réponse informative sur la source." },
  { id: "lx109", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "It's anybody's guess who will win the election.", o: ["Everybody guessed correctly last time.", "The results were announced at noon.", "I'm sure the favorite will win easily.", "True, the polls are too close to call."], a: 3, x: "« anybody's guess » = personne ne sait." },
  { id: "lx110", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "Would you care for a refill?", o: ["The cup was already cracked.", "I filled out the form this morning.", "The refill was free last time.", "Yes, please. Just half a cup."], a: 3, x: "« Would you care for » = voulez-vous ? (offre polie)." },
  { id: "lx111", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "Where's the nearest ATM?", o: ["I withdrew some cash yesterday.", "Inside the lobby, next to the elevators.", "At around five o'clock.", "The machine is very modern."], a: 1, x: "« Where » → un lieu." },
  { id: "lx112", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "The lecture was fascinating, though I could've done without the three-hour length.", o: ["Tell me about it. My legs went numb.", "I did without lunch, too.", "It lasted until three.", "I'm sure it lasted longer than that."], a: 0, x: "« Tell me about it » = j'en sais quelque chose (accord)." },
  { id: "lx113", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Do you mind if I ask you a personal question?", o: ["Go ahead, though I might not answer.", "The question was on the exam.", "I asked her the same one yesterday.", "Yes, that's a very personal question."], a: 0, x: "Question de politesse : « Go ahead » = vas-y." },
  { id: "lx114", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Between you and me, I think the department is in for some big changes.", o: ["I'm in for a quiet semester, I hope.", "The meeting is on Friday.", "I've picked up on that, too. People have been whispering.", "Between us, I told no one."], a: 2, x: "« Between you and me » = confidence → confirmation." },
  { id: "lx115", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Did you get a chance to look at my draft?", o: ["I got a chance to travel last year.", "There's a cold draft in here.", "I did. Overall it's good, but the intro needs work.", "I haven't written one yet."], a: 2, x: "« get a chance » = trouver le temps. Réponse avec retour." },
  { id: "lx116", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "I was hoping to extend my library loan.", o: ["I took out a student loan last year.", "The library closes early on Saturdays.", "Yes, I'm hoping to find that book as well.", "You can renew it online if no one has requested it."], a: 3, x: "« I was hoping to… » = demande indirecte → procédure." },
  { id: "lx117", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "Do you want to share a taxi?", o: ["I took one yesterday, and it cost a lot.", "Good idea. We're going the same way.", "I don't share my secrets with strangers.", "The taxi stand is around the corner."], a: 1, x: "Proposition → acceptation." },
  { id: "lx118", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "I'd like to open a savings account.", o: ["Our interest rates went down last month.", "The account was closed yesterday.", "Certainly. Do you have some form of ID with you?", "Savings are a good idea, thanks."], a: 2, x: "Contexte banque : le conseiller demande les documents nécessaires." },
  { id: "lx119", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Is there a discount for students?", o: ["Yes, ten percent with a valid ID.", "I paid the full price last time.", "Students are welcome on weekends.", "I think the prices have gone up."], a: 0, x: "Question oui/non → oui + condition." },
  { id: "lx120", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Do you want to split an appetizer?", o: ["The appetizers come with bread.", "Sure. How about the spinach dip?", "I already had an appetizer at home.", "I split the check last time."], a: 1, x: "Proposition au restaurant → acceptation + choix." },
  { id: "lx121", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "The more I think about it, the less sense the plan makes.", o: ["I think the plan makes a lot of sense.", "That's what I've been saying all along.", "A good plan takes a lot of thinking.", "I'll think about the lesson later."], a: 1, x: "Corrélatif (« the more…, the less… ») → accord." },
  { id: "lx122", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "What did the doctor say about your knee?", o: ["The knee is very sore.", "I have a doctor's appointment on Monday.", "She said it on Monday.", "I should rest it for two weeks, no running."], a: 3, x: "Discours rapporté : on répond par le contenu du conseil." },
  { id: "lx123", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "It's about time the university upgraded the dining hall.", o: ["The dining hall opens at seven.", "It takes about an hour.", "The hall has been repainted.", "Agreed. The food hasn't changed in years."], a: 3, x: "« It's about time » = il était temps → accord." },
  { id: "lx124", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "Whatever you do, don't mention the layoffs to the interns.", o: ["I mentioned it to the interns yesterday.", "My lips are sealed.", "The interns are late.", "I do whatever I want."], a: 1, x: "Consigne de discrétion → promesse." },
  { id: "lx125", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "I'm having second thoughts about the trip.", o: ["The trip lasts about a week.", "Trips like this are usually a lot of fun.", "Is it the cost, or something else?", "I thought twice about the second cup."], a: 2, x: "Hésitation → question de clarification." },
  { id: "lx126", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "Did you remember to bring your textbook today?", o: ["I took the book home.", "The text was very long.", "Today is a holiday.", "Yes, but I forgot my notebook."], a: 3, x: "Question au passé → réponse + nuance." },
  { id: "lx127", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "I'd be lying if I said I wasn't a little disappointed.", o: ["That's the best news I've heard all week.", "You were right to tell the truth.", "I can tell. Do you want to talk about it?", "Say it again, please."], a: 2, x: "Aveu émotionnel → réponse empathique." },
  { id: "lx128", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "I'm calling about the apartment you advertised.", o: ["I called you yesterday.", "The ad was in the paper.", "It's about an apartment.", "Yes, it's still available. Would you like to see it?"], a: 3, x: "Contexte location : réponse de l'agent." },
  { id: "lx129", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "I forgot to bring my laptop charger.", o: ["You can use mine. I'm not using it right now.", "I forgot to charge mine as well.", "The charger is heavy, isn't it?", "The charge was twenty dollars."], a: 0, x: "Problème → offre d'aide." },
  { id: "lx130", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "How many credits are you taking this semester?", o: ["I take the bus to campus.", "Mostly in the evenings.", "Fifteen, so I'm pretty busy.", "I'll finish them by December."], a: 2, x: "« How many » → un nombre." },
  { id: "lx131", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "I might as well join the study group, since I'm not getting anywhere on my own.", o: ["You'd be better off studying alone, then.", "I joined the group last semester but left.", "That's the spirit. We meet on Tuesdays.", "I might not make it."], a: 2, x: "« might as well » = autant le faire → encouragement." },
  { id: "lx132", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "You can't be serious about moving to Alaska.", o: ["I'm serious about my studies.", "Alaska is very cold.", "Moving is a verb.", "I am. I've already found a job there."], a: 3, x: "Incrédulité → confirmation avec argument." },
  { id: "lx133", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "I'm not too keen on the idea of working all weekend.", o: ["Me neither. Can we split the work with Dan?", "I'm very keen to start tomorrow.", "Weekends are the best time to work, in my opinion.", "The idea is brilliant."], a: 0, x: "« not too keen on » = peu enthousiaste → solution." },
  { id: "lx134", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "Would you like to see the dessert menu?", o: ["The dessert was delicious last time.", "I've already seen the main menu.", "Yes, I'd like to see you.", "Just coffee for me, thanks."], a: 3, x: "Question au restaurant → refus poli avec alternative." },
  { id: "lx135", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "What do you usually do on weekends?", o: ["I did it last weekend.", "The weekend is two days.", "Yes, I do.", "I usually go hiking with some friends."], a: 3, x: "« What do you do » → habitudes (présent simple)." },
  { id: "lx136", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Please remind me to send that email before I leave.", o: ["I remember the deadline.", "Please leave it here.", "Will do. I'll nudge you at four.", "I reminded him yesterday."], a: 2, x: "« Will do » = d'accord, je le ferai." },
  { id: "lx137", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "What kind of music do you usually listen to when you study?", o: ["I like it very much, thanks.", "The music starts at eight.", "Mostly jazz, and some classical.", "I played it yesterday."], a: 2, x: "« What kind of » → une catégorie." },
  { id: "lx138", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "I'm swamped with assignments at the moment.", o: ["I swim every morning.", "Why not ask for an extension on one of them?", "Now is a great moment to start more.", "I assigned the reading myself."], a: 1, x: "« swamped » = débordé → suggestion." },
  { id: "lx139", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "I'm afraid this seat is reserved.", o: ["I'm afraid of heights, too.", "I reserved a table last night.", "Oh, sorry. I'll find another one.", "It's very comfortable, thanks."], a: 2, x: "Remarque polie → excuse et solution." },
  { id: "lx140", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "The new policy goes into effect on the first of the month.", o: ["It has no side effects.", "I'm going into the office on Monday.", "The first of May is nice.", "That doesn't leave us much time to adjust."], a: 3, x: "Annonce → réaction sur le délai." },
  { id: "lx141", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "Looking back, I should've asked for help sooner.", o: ["Hindsight is twenty-twenty, as they say.", "I asked for help just yesterday.", "I looked back at my notes.", "You'll have to look back to find it."], a: 0, x: "Idiome (« hindsight is 20/20 ») → réconfort." },
  { id: "lx142", diff: 3, g: "W", p: "We're a little short-staffed this week.", o: ["In that case, I can stay late on Thursday.", "The staff meeting is on Monday.", "I'm on the staff of the school paper.", "This week has been very long."], a: 0, x: "« short-staffed » = en sous-effectif → offre d'aide." },
  { id: "lx143", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "I'd steer clear of that professor if I were you.", o: ["Her office is on the top floor.", "Clear skies are expected today.", "Really? I was about to sign up for her seminar.", "If I were you, I would, too."], a: 2, x: "Conseil d'éviter → surprise et question." },
  { id: "lx144", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "Is it all right if I turn on the heater?", o: ["Sure, it's freezing in here.", "The heater was installed in July.", "Yes, I turned it up an hour ago.", "Right, let's hear it all."], a: 0, x: "Demande de permission → accord avec justification." },
  { id: "lx145", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "Given the circumstances, I think we did the best we could.", o: ["The circumstances were very bad.", "I suppose so, but I wish we'd had more time.", "Yes, we could have done it.", "The best result is the last one."], a: 1, x: "Bilan résigné, avec un regret." },
  { id: "lx146", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "I didn't think it'd be so hard to find a parking space on campus.", o: ["I thought about it for hours.", "I got a parking permit last week.", "I parked the bike.", "You have to arrive before eight, or forget it."], a: 3, x: "Constat → conseil expérimenté." },
  { id: "lx147", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "I'd like a window seat, if possible.", o: ["I sit by the door.", "The window is open.", "Let me see what's available on that flight.", "Yes, I'd like that too."], a: 2, x: "Contexte voyage : agent qui vérifie la disponibilité." },
  { id: "lx148", diff: 3, g: "M", p: "I could use some fresh air after that meeting.", o: ["The air conditioning is broken in here.", "Let's take a walk around the quad.", "Let's schedule another meeting for Friday.", "The meeting ran an hour over."], a: 1, x: "« I could use » = j'aurais bien besoin de → suggestion." },
  { id: "lx149", diff: 2, g: "M", p: "You wouldn't happen to know where the dean's office is, would you?", o: ["No, I wouldn't mind.", "It's on the top floor, at the end of the hall.", "The dean's secretary is out today.", "I happen to love this place."], a: 1, x: "Question indirecte polie → donner le lieu." },
  { id: "lx150", diff: 2, g: "W", p: "She's been burning the candle at both ends lately.", o: ["She lit a candle in church.", "She'll finish the work by Friday.", "No wonder she looks so tired.", "She bought new candles yesterday."], a: 2, x: "Idiome : s'épuiser → réaction logique (« No wonder »)." }
);

CONTENT.ann.push(
  {"id":"nx001","diff":2,"g":"W","ctx":"Listen to an announcement at a campus bookstore.","text":"Good morning, shoppers, and welcome to the campus bookstore. This week only, we're offering twenty percent off all notebooks, pens, and backpacks, so it's a great time to stock up before the midterm rush. Students who show a valid ID will receive an extra five dollars off any purchase over fifty dollars. The sale ends on Sunday at closing time, and it cannot be combined with any other coupon. Please note that textbooks are not included in this offer, but used copies are available on the second floor at much lower prices. We've also opened a new coffee corner near the entrance, where you can relax between classes. Thank you for shopping with us.","qs":[{"q":"What is the announcement mainly about?","o":["A change in store hours","A new textbook policy","A weekly sale at the bookstore","A job opening"],"a":2,"x":"Promotion de la semaine."},{"q":"What extra benefit do students with ID receive?","o":["A free notebook","Free coffee","Twenty percent off textbooks","Five dollars off a purchase over fifty dollars"],"a":3,"x":"« an extra five dollars off any purchase over fifty dollars »."},{"q":"Where can students find cheaper textbooks?","o":["On the second floor","At the coffee corner","Near the entrance","Online only"],"a":0,"x":"Exemplaires d'occasion au 2e étage."}]},
  {"id":"nx002","diff":2,"g":"M","ctx":"Listen to an announcement at a train station.","text":"Attention, passengers. The ten forty express train to Boston has been delayed by about twenty minutes because of a signal problem outside the city. Our engineers are working on it, and we expect normal service to resume later this afternoon. The train will now depart from platform four instead of platform two, so passengers who have already gone to platform two should walk down the stairs and follow the signs. Please keep your luggage with you at all times. We apologize for the inconvenience this has caused. Information about connecting trains and refunds is available at the service desk in the main hall, where staff will be happy to help you rebook if you miss a connection.","qs":[{"q":"Why is the train late?","o":["Bad weather","A signal problem","A shortage of drivers","Track repairs at the station"],"a":1,"x":"« a signal problem outside the city »."},{"q":"What has changed about the departure?","o":["The destination","The ticket price","The platform","The driver"],"a":2,"x":"Quai 4 au lieu du quai 2."},{"q":"Where can passengers learn about connecting trains?","o":["At the service desk","On platform four","On the website","From the driver"],"a":0,"x":"« at the service desk in the main hall »."}]},
  {"id":"nx003","diff":2,"g":"W","ctx":"Listen to an announcement from the student housing office.","text":"Hello, residents. This is a reminder that the annual fire safety inspection will take place on Tuesday between nine and four. Inspectors will visit every room, so if you'll be at class, please leave your door unlocked. You don't need to be present while they check. However, any items blocking exits or heaters will be reported to the housing office, and you may receive a warning. Also, candles are not allowed in the residence, and neither are extension cords with more than four outlets, so any you have will be removed during the inspection. You can collect the cords from the housing office afterward. If you have questions, stop by the office or send us an email.","qs":[{"q":"What will happen on Tuesday?","o":["A safety inspection of the rooms","A fire drill","A cleaning of the heaters","A meeting for residents"],"a":0,"x":"Inspection annuelle de sécurité incendie."},{"q":"What can residents do if they will be at class?","o":["Give their key to the inspector","Leave their door unlocked","Reschedule the inspection","Ask a friend to be present"],"a":1,"x":"« please leave your door unlocked »."},{"q":"What might be removed from rooms?","o":["Candles and large extension cords","Heaters","Exit signs","Blankets"],"a":0,"x":"Bougies et rallonges de plus de 4 prises."},{"q":"What does the speaker imply about attending the inspection?","o":["It is mandatory for all students","It is only for new residents","It must be arranged in advance","It is not necessary to be there"],"a":3,"x":"« You don't need to be present »."}]},
  {"id":"nx004","diff":2,"g":"M","ctx":"Listen to an announcement at a company staff meeting.","text":"Good morning, team. A few updates before we begin. First, our quarterly sales figures are in, and we exceeded our target by eight percent, which is largely thanks to the hard work of the regional offices, so congratulations to everyone. Second, because of the renovation, the third floor kitchen will be closed for two weeks starting Monday. Please use the one on the fifth floor in the meantime, and apologies for the extra walk. Finally, the annual performance reviews will take place next month. Your manager will send you a calendar invitation by the end of this week, so keep an eye on your inbox, and let me know if the time doesn't suit you.","qs":[{"q":"What is the good news announced?","o":["Sales exceeded the target","A new office opening","A salary increase","A holiday bonus"],"a":0,"x":"Objectif dépassé de 8 %."},{"q":"Why will the third floor kitchen be closed?","o":["It is too dirty","There is a staff shortage","It is being renovated","It is being converted into an office"],"a":2,"x":"« because of the renovation »."},{"q":"What should employees do this week in connection with the performance reviews?","o":["Submit a self-evaluation","Move to the fifth floor","Meet their manager","Watch for a calendar invitation"],"a":3,"x":"« keep an eye on your inbox » : l'invitation arrive d'ici la fin de la semaine."}]},
  {"id":"nx005","diff":3,"g":"W","ctx":"Listen to an announcement from the university registrar.","text":"Good afternoon. I'd like to clarify the recent change to the course withdrawal policy, since I know it has caused some confusion. Previously, students could withdraw from a class up to the tenth week without any record on their transcript. Beginning next term, a withdrawal after the sixth week will appear as a W on the transcript, although it won't affect your grade point average. The change is intended to encourage students to make decisions earlier rather than staying in courses they're unlikely to complete. Exceptions will still be considered for documented medical or family emergencies. Please consult your advisor if you're unsure how this affects your plans, and do so well before the sixth week arrives.","qs":[{"q":"What is the main purpose of the announcement?","o":["To announce new courses","To change the grading scale","To explain a change in withdrawal policy","To remind students of deadlines"],"a":2,"x":"Clarification de la nouvelle politique de retrait."},{"q":"What will happen if a student withdraws in week eight next term?","o":["Nothing will appear on the transcript","The GPA will drop","A W will appear on the transcript","The student will need approval"],"a":2,"x":"Retrait après la semaine 6 → mention W."},{"q":"Why was the policy changed?","o":["To increase tuition income","To reduce the number of courses","To encourage earlier decisions","To protect GPAs"],"a":2,"x":"Encourager les décisions plus tôt."},{"q":"Who might still receive an exception?","o":["Students who are failing","Students with documented emergencies","Students in their final year","Students with advisors' approval only"],"a":1,"x":"Urgences médicales ou familiales documentées."}]},
  {"id":"nx006","diff":2,"g":"M","ctx":"Listen to an announcement on an airplane.","text":"Ladies and gentlemen, this is your captain speaking. We've started our descent into Denver, and we expect to land in about thirty minutes. The weather in Denver is clear, with a temperature of twelve degrees Celsius. We'll be a few minutes ahead of schedule thanks to a strong tailwind, and I'd like to thank you for your patience during the turbulence earlier. The flight attendants will be coming through the cabin to collect any trash. Please make sure your seat backs and tray tables are in the upright position, and keep your seat belt fastened until the sign is turned off after we reach the gate. Thank you for flying with us, and we hope to see you again soon.","qs":[{"q":"When will the plane land?","o":["In about ten minutes","In about thirty minutes","In about an hour","Right now"],"a":1,"x":"« in about thirty minutes »."},{"q":"Why will the flight arrive early?","o":["A tailwind is helping","The plane is flying faster by design","There is little traffic at the airport","The route was changed"],"a":0,"x":"« a strong tailwind »."},{"q":"What should passengers do now?","o":["Put their seats and tray tables upright","Collect their luggage","Walk to the gate","Fill out a form"],"a":0,"x":"Dossiers et tablettes en position verticale."}]},
  {"id":"nx007","diff":3,"g":"W","ctx":"Listen to an announcement made by a conference organizer.","text":"Welcome back, everyone, and thank you for your patience. I'm afraid the keynote speaker, Dr. Hall, has been held up at the airport because of fog, so we've had to rearrange this afternoon's program. Instead of her address at two, we'll begin with the panel on research funding, which was originally scheduled for four. Dr. Hall is now expected to arrive around five and will speak at six, right before the closing dinner. Those of you who planned to leave early might want to adjust your travel plans, as the final session will now run later than advertised. Please also note that the closing dinner has been moved to the garden room. Updated printed programs are available at the registration desk.","qs":[{"q":"Why was the program changed?","o":["A room was unavailable","A speaker was delayed","The panel was cancelled","There was a power failure"],"a":1,"x":"Intervenante retenue à l'aéroport à cause du brouillard."},{"q":"What will take place at two?","o":["The keynote address","The closing dinner","The panel on research funding","A coffee break"],"a":2,"x":"Le panel est avancé à 14 h."},{"q":"What does the organizer suggest to people who planned to leave early?","o":["Skip the panel","Attend the dinner","Change their travel arrangements","Contact Dr. Hall"],"a":2,"x":"« might want to adjust your travel plans »."},{"q":"What else has changed?","o":["The date of the conference","The title of the keynote","The panel members","The location of the dinner"],"a":3,"x":"Dîner dans la « garden room »."}]},
  {"id":"nx008","diff":2,"g":"M","ctx":"Listen to an announcement at a university gym.","text":"Hi, everyone. Starting next Monday, the gym will have new opening hours. We'll open at six in the morning and close at ten at night, Monday through Friday, which should suit those of you with early classes. On weekends, we'll be open from eight to six. We're also starting free yoga classes every Wednesday at noon, led by one of our certified instructors. You don't need to register, but spaces are limited, so try to arrive a few minutes early, and just bring your own mat. Please remember to wipe down the machines after you use them, and thanks to everyone who has been doing that already. Have a great workout.","qs":[{"q":"What is changing next Monday?","o":["The membership fee","The equipment","The gym hours","The staff"],"a":2,"x":"Nouveaux horaires."},{"q":"When will the yoga classes take place?","o":["Every Monday morning","Saturdays at six","Fridays at ten","Wednesdays at noon"],"a":3,"x":"« every Wednesday at noon »."},{"q":"What should people bring to yoga?","o":["A registration form","A towel","Water only","Their own mat"],"a":3,"x":"« just bring your own mat »."}]},
  {"id":"nx009","diff":2,"g":"W","ctx":"Listen to an announcement at the start of a workshop.","text":"Welcome, everyone, to today's workshop on academic writing. Before we begin, I'd like to go over a few details. The session will last about two hours, with a ten-minute break halfway through. Handouts are on the table by the door, and the slides will be emailed to you afterward, so there's no need to photograph them. We'll spend the first hour on structuring an argument and the second on citing sources, drawing on real examples from past student essays. If you have a draft with you, feel free to use it in the exercises. Questions are welcome at any time, but if we run short of time, I'll answer the remaining ones by email.","qs":[{"q":"How long is the workshop?","o":["About one hour","About two hours","About three hours","All day"],"a":1,"x":"« about two hours »."},{"q":"How will participants get the slides?","o":["From the table","By email afterward","On the website","They will not get them"],"a":1,"x":"« emailed to you afterward »."},{"q":"What will be covered in the second hour?","o":["Citing sources","Structuring an argument","Editing drafts","Presentations"],"a":0,"x":"2e heure : citer des sources."},{"q":"What does the speaker suggest participants may do with their drafts?","o":["Hand them in","Use them in exercises","Throw them away","Submit them online"],"a":1,"x":"« feel free to use it in the exercises »."}]},
  {"id":"nx010","diff":3,"g":"M","ctx":"Listen to an announcement from a city transit authority.","text":"This is a service notice for commuters. Beginning the first of next month, the transit authority will introduce a new fare system. Instead of paying per trip, riders will be charged a daily fare that is capped at six dollars, regardless of how many journeys they make. Monthly passes will remain available, but their price will increase by about four percent. Officials say the change is meant to simplify payment and make short, frequent trips cheaper. Riders who currently hold prepaid cards will have their balance carried over automatically, and no action is necessary. More details can be found on the authority's website, and extra staff will be on hand at the busiest stations during the first week to answer questions.","qs":[{"q":"What change is being announced?","o":["The end of monthly passes","New bus routes","A fare freeze","A new fare system with a daily cap"],"a":3,"x":"Tarif journalier plafonné à 6 $."},{"q":"What will happen to monthly passes?","o":["They will be discontinued","They will be free","They will stay at the same price","They will cost slightly more"],"a":3,"x":"Hausse d'environ 4 %."},{"q":"Who benefits most from the new system?","o":["People who take few, long trips","People who make several short trips a day","Tourists","Monthly pass holders"],"a":1,"x":"Trajets courts et fréquents moins chers."},{"q":"What must current prepaid card holders do?","o":["Nothing","Register online","Exchange their cards","Pay a fee"],"a":0,"x":"« no action is necessary »."}]},
  {"id":"nx011","diff":2,"g":"W","ctx":"Listen to an announcement by a student club president.","text":"Hi, everyone, and thanks for coming to the first meeting of the semester. I have a few quick announcements. Our hiking trip to Red Rock Canyon is scheduled for the second Saturday of October. The cost is fifteen dollars, which covers transportation and lunch, and you can pay at the next meeting. Please wear sturdy shoes and bring at least two liters of water, because there's no shop on the trail. We're also looking for someone to take over as treasurer, since Priya is graduating. If you're interested, please talk to me after the meeting. Last, we're collecting donations of used hiking boots for a local youth program, so check your closets before you buy anything new.","qs":[{"q":"What does the fifteen dollars cover?","o":["Equipment rental","Club membership","Camping fees","Transportation and lunch"],"a":3,"x":"Transport et déjeuner."},{"q":"Why does the club need a new treasurer?","o":["Priya is graduating","Priya is traveling","Nobody wants the job","The club is closing"],"a":0,"x":"Priya termine ses études."},{"q":"What are members asked to donate?","o":["Money","Used hiking boots","Backpacks","Food"],"a":1,"x":"Vieilles chaussures de randonnée."}]},
  {"id":"nx012","diff":3,"g":"M","ctx":"Listen to an announcement from a university IT department.","text":"This is a message from the IT department regarding scheduled maintenance. On Saturday night, from eleven p.m. until about five a.m., the student portal, email, and the online library catalog will be unavailable while we upgrade our servers. Although the work is expected to finish by five, there's a small chance of delays, so please don't count on access early Sunday morning. If you have an assignment due on Sunday, we strongly recommend submitting it before Saturday evening, as instructors have been told that technical downtime won't be accepted as an excuse for late work. The campus Wi-Fi will not be affected, and the IT help desk will answer questions by phone until ten on Saturday evening.","qs":[{"q":"What will be unavailable during the maintenance?","o":["The student portal, email, and library catalog","Campus Wi-Fi","All computers on campus","Only email"],"a":0,"x":"Portail, e-mail et catalogue."},{"q":"What does the speaker advise students with Sunday deadlines to do?","o":["Ask for an extension","Use the Wi-Fi","Submit work before Saturday evening","Contact IT"],"a":2,"x":"Rendre le travail avant samedi soir."},{"q":"What does the speaker imply about late assignments?","o":["Instructors will be flexible about downtime","Late work will be graded higher","Downtime will not excuse lateness","The deadline will be moved automatically"],"a":2,"x":"« won't be accepted as an excuse »."},{"q":"Why does the speaker say not to count on access early Sunday?","o":["The portal closes permanently","The work may take longer than planned","The campus is closed","Servers are being replaced for good"],"a":1,"x":"Risque de retard."}]},
  {"id":"nx013","diff":2,"g":"W","ctx":"Listen to an announcement in a campus dining hall.","text":"Hello, students. Please note that the dining hall will close early today, at six instead of eight, because of a staff training session that was scheduled at short notice. Dinner will be served from five to six, and the menu will include the usual vegetarian options. If you have a meal plan, you can also use your card at the snack bar in the student center, which will stay open until midnight. Please keep in mind that the snack bar has a more limited menu, mostly sandwiches and soups. Breakfast will start at seven tomorrow as usual. We apologize for the change, and thank you for your understanding.","qs":[{"q":"Why will the dining hall close early?","o":["A broken oven","A holiday","A power cut","Staff training"],"a":3,"x":"Formation du personnel."},{"q":"Where can students use their meal plan tonight after six?","o":["At the snack bar in the student center","At the library","Nowhere","At the gym"],"a":0,"x":"Snack bar jusqu'à minuit."},{"q":"When does breakfast start tomorrow?","o":["At six","At seven","At eight","At nine"],"a":1,"x":"7 h comme d'habitude."}]},
  {"id":"nx014","diff":3,"g":"M","ctx":"Listen to an announcement by a professor at the end of a course.","text":"As we wrap up, a word about the final project. A number of you have asked whether groups may present remotely. The answer is yes, provided you inform me by Friday and test your connection in advance. However, I'd caution against assuming a remote presentation is easier. In my experience, groups that present online tend to lose the audience's attention more quickly, so you'll need to plan your visuals carefully. Also, I've heard that some of you are planning to combine this project with your capstone. That's fine in principle, but you'll need written approval from both instructors beforehand, and I'd like to see that approval at least two weeks before the presentation date.","qs":[{"q":"Under what condition may groups present remotely?","o":["They must have a medical reason","They must tell the professor by Friday and test their connection","They must present first","They must record the talk"],"a":1,"x":"Prévenir avant vendredi et tester la connexion."},{"q":"What does the professor imply about remote presentations?","o":["They are easier","They are graded more strictly","They are not allowed","They can be harder to keep engaging"],"a":3,"x":"On perd plus vite l'attention."},{"q":"What is required to combine the project with a capstone?","o":["A longer presentation","Approval from both instructors in writing","A new group","Nothing special"],"a":1,"x":"Autorisation écrite des deux enseignants."}]}
);
